    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on levin-2025-wisdom-08: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.73";
    dc:description "Large public genotype-phenotype resources make the channelopathy component highly analysable. The broader symmetry and applicability of all neuroscience tool classes are only partly covered and not uniquely established by shared ion-channel mechanisms.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Systematically estimate enrichment of developmental-patterning phenotypes among pathogenic ion-channel variants and catalogue controlled morphogenetic effects of drugs, optogenetic perturbations and training protocols. Enrichment and reproducible control across modalities support the empirical generalization.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Deep symmetry is interpretive rather than a single endpoint.", "Phenotype annotation and ascertainment vary by gene.", "Training-protocol evidence is much thinner than channelopathy evidence.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.82"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/levin-2025-wisdom-08--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/levin-2025-wisdom-08--gpt--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/levin-2025-wisdom-08--gpt--dataset-3>;
